    "editorial:Content_hi.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "94e32ec653913ea687d6f1c9736c7551fe65ec9a5b1070d9f56642ecb02910a8",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- The mixed facing directions example incorrectly claims that a person facing north and a person facing south in a linear row are \"एक-दूसरे के सामने हैं\" (facing each other); in a row they face perpendicular directions, not each other. The left/right reversal occurs because they face opposite directions, not because they face each other. → Correct the explanation: they face opposite directions, causing their left/right to be reversed relative to each other.",
        "- The mnemonic \"आमने-सामने, दायाँ-बायाँ बदले; पीठ-पीठ, दिशा एक ही दीठ\" and its explanation are misapplied to linear mixed directions; it actually describes face-to-face/back-to-back scenarios (e.g., two parallel rows). In a single row with north/south facing, persons facing opposite directions have reversed left/right, not same. → Clarify that the mnemonic is for face-to-face/back-to-back arrangements; for a row, use the arrow method to determine each person's left/right individually."
      ],
